          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A bialgebroid may be viewed as a multiobject generalization of a concept of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bialgebra"} bialgebra
          %h4#nomenclature Nomenclature
          %p
            This entry is about “associative” bialgebroid, see also the different concept of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+bialgebroid"} Lie bialgebroid
          %h4#motivation_in_tannakian_formalism Motivation in Tannakian formalism
          %p
            When a monoidal category has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+functor"} fiber functor
            to a category of vector spaces over a field, one tries to “reconstruct” the category as the category of representations of the endomorphism object of a fiber functor. One often does not have a fiber functor to vector spaces but only to bimodules over some base algebra
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and the category is equivalent to the category of representations of that bialgebroid.
          %h2#definition Definition
